! mcp_bootstrap_p121.strap -- "IF ANALYZER TABLE OF TENTACLE
! ADDRESSES", printed page 121.  docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF
! p.128, header read and not assumed: the top line prints "TIME
! CLOCK 00054041   PUNID 11011MCP   CARD ID EA000163   DIST. OF
! 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 121".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE CONTAINS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FORTY-NINE LINES, card serials EA000163 (line 1) through
! EA000211 (line 49), counted off the serial column -- forty-nine
! serials for forty-nine lines, so nothing fell off the top or the
! bottom of the render.
!
! Line 4 is a CNOP.  Lines 5-14, 18-27, 31-35 and 39-49 are
! THIRTY-SIX "VF,<name>" half words: a dense table of tentacle
! addresses, one entry per IF-analyzer indicator bit.  The other
! twelve lines (1, 2, 3, 15, 16, 17, 28, 29, 30, 36, 37, 38) are
! comment cards -- LOCATION and BINARY OUTPUT both empty, the card
! printing raw from column 2 so the NAME column is empty and the
! text runs through the STATEMENT column.  They read:
!    1  (blank)
!    2  *****  IF ANALYZER TABLE OF TENTACLE ADDRESSES  *****
!    3  (blank)
!   15  (blank)
!   16  *****  RESERVED FOR FUTURE MCP USE  *****
!   17  (blank)
!   28  (blank)
!   29  ****** RESERVED FOR INSTALLATION PSEUDO OPS ******
!   30  (blank)
!   36  (blank)
!   37  ****** SPECIAL MCP PSEUDO OPS ******
!   38  (blank)
!
! ONE SYMBOL IS DEFINED HERE: MIFTTT, at 215666.00, the table's
! base.  Everything else named on the page is an external.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE JOIN FROM printed p.120, AND WHY THE SLC BELOW IS AN
! ASSERTION RATHER THAN A CHECK
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THIS PAGE PRINTS NO SLC. <<<  Line 4 is a CNOP and line 5 is
! the first row to spend storage.  The SLC written below is
! therefore a hard origin, and docs/transcription_workflow.md
! ("WHAT THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE", point 2) is explicit that a hard
! SLC OVERRIDES the arriving counter silently: move it and all
! thirty-six !CHECK rows move with it and still pass.  So the
! thirty-six checks below do NOT test the join.  What supports it:
!
!   (a) printed p.120 line 14 is "M PRIM Q DRZ(BU,32),(30)" at
!       215647.00 and prints 000017.00 -- 0o17 = 15 words -- so the
!       counter leaves p.120 at 215647 + 15 = 215666.00, and this
!       page's line 5 PRINTS 215666.00.  Two-sided.
!   (b) decks/mcp_bootstrap_p117.strap and _p119.strap both SYN
!       MIFTTT at (8)215666.0, each back-derived from an
!       "LV,n,MIFTTT-64.0($n)" that prints 215566 -- 215666 less
!       0o100 words.  Those two are HALF-WORD granular (limitation
!       1), but they land on the same word, independently, on two
!       pages transcribed separately.
!
! >>> THE !SYM FOR MIFTTT IS CIRCULAR AND IS NOT CORROBORATION.
! <<<  MIFTTT is the first thing the SLC places, so "!SYM MIFTTT
! 215666.00" tests the SLC against itself.  It is declared because
! the page prints that location, not because it proves anything.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE COMMENT COLUMN IS A SECOND, INDEPENDENT READING OF THE
! LOCATION COLUMN, AND IT CLOSES ALL THIRTY-SIX ROWS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Most rows carry a comment of the form "-NN.0" or "-NN.32" -- the
! IF indicator bit the entry serves.  printed p.117 line 40 and
! printed p.119 line 2 both index this table as "MIFTTT-64.0", so
! entry i (0-based from line 5) serves indicator word 64 + i//2,
! bit .0 or .32, and sits at 0o215666 + i//2 word, .00 or .40.
!
! MEASURED OVER ALL THIRTY-SIX ROWS: zero mismatches.  The printed
! LOCATION and the printed English comment agree on every single
! row, and the table is DENSE over indicator addresses 64.0
! through 81.32 -- thirty-six entries, no holes, no duplicates.
! That is what rules out a row having been dropped or doubled
! across the three comment-card gaps (lines 15-17, 28-30, 36-38),
! which no !CHECK can do: a dropped row would shift every later
! location by a half word and break the correspondence.
! Lines 9 and 10 print "-RESUME LOAD." and "-DISK FETCH" with no
! number; the arithmetic puts them at 66.0 and 66.32, between
! line 8's printed "-65.32" and line 11's printed "-67.0".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE BIT OFFSETS OF THESE SIXTEEN EXTERNALS ARE OBSERVED, NOT
! CONVENTIONAL -- THIS PAGE IS THE EXCEPTION TO LIMITATION 1
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! An address back-derived from a branch or an LVI is pinned only to
! the half word, so writing ".00" is a convention.  NOT HERE.  A VF
! compiles its value as a 24-bit-plus-sign quantity (C22-6531
! printed p.18, quoted in strap_asm's VF handler), and 24 bits is
! the whole byte address -- 18 bits of word and 6 of bit offset.
!
! MEASURED rather than assumed, by varying one SYN and assembling:
!
!   SYN value          the VF row prints
!   (8)234417.00       234417.00+
!   (8)234417.03       234417.03+
!   (8)234417.04       234417.04+
!   (8)234417.37       234417.37+
!   (8)234417.40       234417.40+
!
! Every offset shows.  So the ".00" on all sixteen SYNs below is a
! READING off the BINARY OUTPUT column, and the thirty-six !CHECK
! rows really do test it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE SIXTEEN EXTERNALS AND WHERE EACH SPELLING COMES FROM
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The page gives every one of these its address directly, in the
! BINARY OUTPUT column -- nothing here is back-derived.  What
! needed outside evidence was the SPELLING, which listing_oracle
! never checks.  Of the seventeen names on this page (sixteen
! externals plus MIFTTT): TWELVE are corroborated off this page in
! BOTH name and address (MIFTTT, PDUMPT, YJC4TT, POLDTT, YRLTT,
! XTENTB, SASPUT, SCSPRT, VVSCR, SCDRYT, SAEOJT, VVSKM), TWO are
! corroborated by halves (AEDMPT -- address only; JTENT -- name
! only), and THREE rest on this page's ink alone (PDBTT, YJC1TT,
! UNDEF).
!
! tests/check_symbol_spellings.py was RUN with this deck beside the
! ~90 landed ones: "PASS 1076 symbol definitions, no symbol spelled
! two ways."  So none of the seventeen is spelled differently by any
! page already transcribed -- which, for the three that rest on ink,
! means only that no landed deck contradicts them, not that any
! confirms them.
!
!  MIFTTT  215666.00  DEFINED HERE.  Also SYN'd by the landed decks
!                     for pp.117 and 119, and the typeset manual
!                     C22-6728-1 says "The IF analyzer operation
!                     table starts at MIFTTT" -- which is this
!                     page's own title.
!  PDUMPT  234417.00  docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_250-445.txt: a reference
!                     "BB,PDUMPT.4,APUMPB" printed AT 234417.04.
!                     Name and address both.
!  AEDMPT  217460.00  docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt prints a
!                     routine block at 2174xx whose labels are
!                     AEDMP2, AEDMP4, AEDMPI, AEDMP7, and line
!                     "217463.40 ... LV,$0,AEDMPT+3." -- 217460 + 3
!                     = 217463, the row's own word.  ADDRESS
!                     CORROBORATED, spelling only by the AEDMPn
!                     family and this page's "-ERROR DUMP".
!  YJC4TT  231136.00  MCP_Mar63_250-445: a defining card "YJC4TT
!                     DD(BU,12,3),(8)C4C1", and "LVE,$14,YJC4TT+
!                     2.32" printed at 231140.75 -- 231136 + 2.
!  POLDTT  232677.00  MCP_Mar63_250-445: "BZB,P OLD TT+.04,P KOLDL"
!                     printed at 232677.04, and a second reference
!                     "CT0011(BU,32),POLDTT+1.6".
!  YRLTT   232555.00  MCP_Mar63_250-445: a defining card "YRLTT
!                     DD(BU,6),(8)04" and "BZB,YRLTT+2-.50" printed
!                     at 232557.62 -- 232555 + 2.
!  XTENTB  233667.00  MCP_Mar63_250-445: a defining card "XTENTB
!                     DD(BU,45),..." and four references
!                     "BB,XTENTB+.4,..." printed at 233667.04.
!                     The final glyph is B, not 8: read at 1800 dpi
!                     it has a straight vertical LEFT stem with two
!                     bowls, where an 8 closes on the left.
!  SASPUT 222111.00   MCP_Mar63_001-249: "BB,SASPUT.4,RNOCKK"
!                     printed at 222130.40 with 222111.04 in its
!                     binary.  Manual C22-6728-1: "SCSPRT and
!                     SASPUT, each four words in length."
!  SCSPRT 222105.00   MCP_Mar63_001-249: "BB,SCSPRT.4,..." printed
!                     at 222235.00 with 222105.04 in its binary.
!                     Same manual sentence.  The third glyph is a
!                     round C with no left stem, beside the D in
!                     PDBTT and SCDRYT on the same page.
!  VVSCR  224105.00   MCP_Mar63_001-249 prints its defining card,
!                     "224105.00  V VSCR DD(FU,4),3,1"; the manual
!                     names it too.
!  SCDRYT 222120.00   >>> THE INK AND THE OCR DISAGREED AND THE
!                     MANUAL SETTLED IT. <<<  tesseract reads
!                     "SCERYT" in BOTH places it occurs in the
!                     volume OCR (this page's line 40 and the
!                     defining card "222120.00  SCDRYT
!                     DD(BU,4,8),1  -TENTACLE TABLE FOR -OUTPUT-").
!                     At 1800 dpi the fourth glyph has a straight
!                     vertical left stem and a single bowl -- a D
!                     with the bowl worn through, the shape
!                     docs/transcription_workflow.md warns about --
!                     where an E would carry three horizontal bars.
!                     Decided by one grep, not by the glyph:
!                     C22-6728 AND C22-6728-1, two revisions of the
!                     typeset System Analysis Guide, both print
!                     "receives control at CDRY ... via its
!                     tentacle table, SCDRYT."  SCDRYT.
!  SAEOJT 222115.00   MCP_Mar63_001-249 prints its defining card,
!                     "222115.00  SAEOJT DD(BU,4,8),1  -TENTACLE
!                     TABLE FOR EOJ"; manual: "package with an
!                     associated tentacle table (SAEOJT)".
!  PDBTT  232566.00   NOT CORROBORATED ANYWHERE.  Read at 1800 dpi:
!                     P, D (left stem), B (left stem, two bowls),
!                     T, T.  Its comment is "-78.0 DEBUGGER", which
!                     is consistent with P-DeBug-Tentacle-Table but
!                     is not a spelling.
!  VVSKM  224111.00   MCP_Mar63_001-249 prints its defining card,
!                     "224111.00  V VSKM DD(FU,4),2,91  -2
!                     PARAMETERS, ENABLED SIC ENTRY"; manual C22-
!                     6728-1: "the VVSKM tentacle".
!  JTENT  232715.00   MCP_Mar63_250-445 prints a defining card
!                     "J TENT DD(BU,4),5  / NUMBER OF PARAMETERS"
!                     -- the first word of a tentacle table.  NAME
!                     corroborated, ADDRESS not (that OCR line
!                     carries no location).  The glyph is J, not S:
!                     at 1800 dpi it has a bare vertical with a
!                     bottom-left hook, no upper bowl.
!  YJC1TT 230747.00   NOT CORROBORATED ANYWHERE.  Read at 1800 dpi
!                     as YJC1TT beside the page's own thirteen
!                     clean YJC4TT rows; the only difference is the
!                     fifth glyph, 1 against 4.  Its comment is
!                     "-76.32 JC1".
!  UNDEF  233144.00   NOT a transcription of ink alone: all three
!                     rows that use it (47, 48, 49) print the same
!                     address, line 48's D drops its bowl and reads
!                     C while 47 and 49 print it closed, and the
!                     word is English.  It is almost certainly the
!                     assembly's "undefined tentacle" placeholder --
!                     which is what the three comments "LOGGER 4",
!                     "LOGGER 2", "LOGGER 1" being pointed at one
!                     common address says.  NOT corroborated off
!                     the page; recorded as read.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT IS RECORDED AND NOT EXPLAINED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) LINE 4's CNOP PRINTS NO LOCATION AND NO BINARY.  Contrast
!     printed p.120 line 5, where the same op prints "215637.40
!     000000.30 00" because a 24-bit DD had left the counter at
!     .30.  Here the counter arrives word-aligned at 215666.00 and
!     the CNOP emits nothing.  THE CARD IS KEPT IN THE DECK rather
!     than dropped: if strap_asm emitted a no-op unconditionally,
!     every one of the thirty-six rows below would shift by a half
!     word and say so.  (It does not; measured.)
! (2) A BARE "*" AFTER THE LOCATION ON LINE 34 -- "215701.40 *".
!     Line 34 is a VF identical to lines 33 and 35, which print no
!     star.  printed pp.3, 37, 103, 116 and 120 all carry this mark
!     and all leave it unexplained.  It changes no compiled bit.
! (3) ONE CARD SERIAL IS MISSING AT THE JOIN.  printed p.120's last
!     line is card EA000161; this page's line 1 is EA000163.  Card
!     EA000162 produced no listing line on either page.  Recorded,
!     not explained.
! (4) THE NEXT PAGE'S ORIGIN IS NOT 215710.00 ON THIS PAGE'S
!     EVIDENCE ALONE.  Line 49 is a VF at 215707.40, and by the
!     same C22-6531 sentence quoted above the counter stands at BIT
!     25 of that half word when the page ends.  MEASURED, by
!     appending "ZEND SYN,$" to this deck and assembling: the
!     counter is at 215707.71 -- 0o71 = 0o40 + 25 -- NOT 215710.00.
!     It becomes 215710.00 only when whatever printed p.122
!     compiles first rounds it up, which every item except another
!     VF does.  Compare by hand when p.122 lands; if p.122 prints
!     an "SLC,$" its printed LOCATION is the free witness.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT IS CHECKED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ALL THIRTY-SIX location-bearing rows carry a !CHECK, and the one
! symbol the page defines carries a !SYM.  There is no DRZ, no SYN
! and no bare-octal DD on this page, so there is no row with a
! printed value that a check cannot consume.  Only line 4 (the
! silent CNOP) and the twelve comment cards are unchecked, and
! neither prints anything to check.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! TWO THINGS THE NEXT PERSON NEEDS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (a) MIFTTT IS NOW DEFINED TWICE OVER THE MERGED IMAGE.  The
!     landed decks for printed pp.117 and 119 each carry
!     "MIFTTT SYN,(8)215666.0" as an external; THIS page defines
!     the label.  All three agree on the word, so nothing is
!     wrong -- but strap/mcp_image.py will see a duplicate
!     definition when these three pages merge, and the two SYNs
!     are the ones to drop, not this definition.
! (b) THE SURVEY'S OCR OF THIS PAGE UNDER-READS, as its own
!     calibration says it does.  It reported 26 rows carrying a
!     LOCATION over 215666.00..215704.00.  Read by eye the page has
!     THIRTY-SIX, over 215666.00..215707.40.  The start agrees
!     exactly; the end is three words short because the OCR lost
!     rows near the bottom.  Its "0 rows with a trailing +" is also
!     correct and is NOT evidence against this being code: every
!     "+" on this page is in the BINARY OUTPUT column, where it is
!     a VF's sign, and the LOCATION column carries none.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

