! >>> LINES 11 AND 12 PUNCH THEIR OPERAND WITH AN EMBEDDED BLANK,
! AND strap_asm REJECTS THE PRINTED FORM.  TESTED, NOT ASSUMED. <<<
! The cards read "VF,S ASPUT" and "VF,S CSPRT".  Assembling the
! printed form verbatim:
!
!   SASPUT  SYN, (8)222111.00
!           SLC, (8)215671.
!           VF, S ASPUT
!   -> AssemblerError line 3: undefined symbol 'S'
!
! strap_asm takes "S" as the whole operand and stops.  IBM's own
! assembler did not: C22-6531 printed p.10 limits a symbol to SIX
! characters, and docs/NEXT.md records fifteen MCP names that are
! legal ONLY once their blanks are removed, so STRAP ignores
! embedded blanks in a symbol.  SASPUT and SCSPRT are six
! characters exactly, which is the same arithmetic.
!
! So the deck above substitutes the closed-up spellings -- the ones
! the typeset manual C22-6728-1 also uses -- and they assemble
! BIT-IDENTICALLY, as rows 11 and 12 of the !CHECK block show
! (222111.00+ and 222105.00+, both passing).  The printed form is
! kept in those two !CHECK notes.  FLAGGED as a strap_asm gap: it
